<title>UK: Abbot Group unit sells two oil rigs.</title>
<headline>Abbot Group unit sells two oil rigs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Abbot Group Plc said on Tuesday its subsidiary KCA had sold two loss-making land rigs for a total $2.2 million in cash to West coast International Oilfield Rentals BV of the Netherlands.</p>
<p>The rigs had a book value of about 900,000 stg.</p>
<p>The proceeds of the sale, which is expected to be concluded by th end of this month, will be used to reduce net borrowings.</p>
<p>The sale will enable KCA to concentrate on its activities in North Africa and the Caspian Sea in particular, said Abbott.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
